#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md:13
msgid ""
"Each accepts a positive integer **or** `auto`. `auto` is a value you can "
"write, not merely the absence of one: it is how a level is put back to "
"automatic after a configuration file or an environment variable has "
"pinned it to a number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md:17
msgid ""
"Zero and negatives are a typed error naming the option you mistyped. From"
" a configuration file the same two levels are `n_workers` and the "
"`parallelism` section:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md:27
msgid "The two parallelism levels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md:28
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**Jobs run in separate processes.** Loading a PDF goes through PyMuPDF, "
"which means through Python, which means through the GIL — profiling put "
"that load at 35–75% of a job's wall time. Threads would have re-"
"serialised exactly the part worth parallelising. The children report "
"their results back to the parent, which writes the output once, so "
"process-level parallelism does not change what is produced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md:34
msgid ""
"**Pages of one document run in threads**, on a pool the crate owns rather"
" than rayon's global one, so that a program embedding the crate keeps its"
" own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md:37
msgid ""
"`-j 1` therefore has a universal meaning: one job at a time *and* one "
"page at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md:39
msgid "What parallelism buys, and what it costs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md:40
msgid "Measured on a 20-thread machine, two large reports in one run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md
msgid "Time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md
msgid "Note"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md
msgid "sequential"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md
msgid "39.4 s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md
msgid "defaults"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md
msgid "16.7 s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md
msgid "**2.36×**, output byte-identical to sequential"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md:47
msgid ""
"Page-level threading alone gave 4.4–7.0× *inside the engine*; the end-to-"
"end figure is lower because the PDF loading that only job-level "
"parallelism touches remains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md:50
msgid ""
"The price is **memory**: peak went from 783 MB to about 1.2 GB for two "
"concurrent large jobs, and it grows with the number of jobs running at "
"once. On a memory-constrained machine, `--jobs 1` keeps page-level "
"threading and drops the concurrent copies of the document — usually the "
"right trade, since it gives up the smaller of the two gains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md:55
msgid "When a format does not speed up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md:57
msgid ""
"A format whose work is done by an author's Python pipe does not scale "
"with threads, and **says so**: those pipes declare that they do not, and "
"the engine runs them sequentially rather than contending for the GIL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md:61
msgid ""
"A format that gains nothing from `--pages` is usually one of these. That "
"is the design working, not failing — the alternative is threads that "
"queue on the GIL and cost more than they save. Measured: one small format"
" with an author's `deserialize` went 182 ms → 189 ms between one thread "
"and twenty, while an entirely structured format went 7.2 s → 1.0 s on the"
" same machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md:66
msgid "Reproducibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md:68
msgid ""
"Parallelism does not change the tables. Results from the jobs are "
"collected in **indexed slots**, so the aggregated output is byte-"
"identical whether you run at one worker or twenty — verified in the test "
"suite, and by checksum against the reference outputs of the formats "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/parallelism.md:72
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The one place the ordering guarantee is spent is the **merging of log "
"files**, where the children's lines are poured into the parent's in job "
"order rather than in the instant they happened. See "
"{doc}`../../../reference/design/determinism`."
msgstr ""

